<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">People's Republic of Zanzibar</h1><p class="st-meta">1964 CE – 1964 CE · capital Zanzibar City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The revolutionary state born in Zanzibar's violent overthrow of the sultan in January 1964, which lasted three months before union with Tanganyika.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>A month after the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Sultanate of Zanzibar</a> became independent, on 12 January 1964 an uprising led by the Ugandan-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-okello">John Okello</a> and supporters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party">Afro-Shirazi Party</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamshid-bin-abdullah">Sultan Jamshid bin Abdullah</a> and the Arab-dominated government. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume">Abeid Karume</a> of the Afro-Shirazi Party became president of the People's Republic of Zanzibar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemba-island">Pemba</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The revolution was accompanied by mass killings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> and South Asians, with thousands dead, and the confiscation of property. A Revolutionary Council ruled by decree, and the new state turned to the Soviet bloc, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">East Germany</a> for support, raising Western fears of an African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 26 April 1964 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume">Karume</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tanganyika">Tanganyika</a> to form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-republic-of-tanganyika-and-zanzibar">United Republic</a>, later named <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tanzania">Tanzania</a>. Zanzibar kept its own president and government within the union.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/peoples-republic-of-zanzibar.jpg" alt="People's Republic of Zanzibar" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SuperManu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zanzibar_(January-April_1964).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1964 CE – 1964 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zanzibar City</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abeid Karume</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swahili</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tanzania">Tanzania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>People's Republic of Zanzibar and Pemba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=peoples-republic-of-zanzibar" aria-label="People's Republic of Zanzibar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5766 2408 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where People's Republic of Zanzibar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6086 2664L6086 2664M6086 2664L5990 2665"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6086 2664h0M5990 2665h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6086 2664h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6086 2664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Zanzibar City. <a href="/atlas?year=1964&amp;focus=peoples-republic-of-zanzibar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
